//@version=6
indicator("OHLC4 Structure Ribbon [RMA] ", "OHLC4 Ribbon", overlay=true, calc_bars_count=2500, max_bars_back=5000, max_labels_count=500)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Script Overview
// ==============================================================================================
//
// OHLC STACK RIBBON — MULTI-HORIZON RMA(OHLC4) STRUCTURE
//
// WHAT THIS INDICATOR DOES
// • Builds a six-average structural ribbon from Wilder RMA applied to OHLC4:
//      5 / 8 / 13 / 20 / 34 / 50.
// • Uses the shape, ordering, and directional strength of the full stack to classify market structure.
// • Separates short/intermediate ribbon structure from a slower 75 / 110 RMA(OHLC4) structural pair.
// • Adds regime-colored candles, right-side level labels, persistent price-cross arrows,
//   crossover event labels, a two-bar price follow line, and a compact two-row context table.
//
// CORE ENGINE
//
// 1) REG BODY — regression-derived ribbon body
// • Each of the six RMA horizons is assigned its theoretical Wilder-RMA lag:
//      5→4, 8→7, 13→12, 20→19, 34→33, 50→49 bars.
// • A linear regression across those lag coordinates estimates the directional slope of the entire stack.
// • That slope is projected across the full lag span to create one signed structural spread:
//      positive = faster horizons are structurally above slower horizons;
//      negative = faster horizons are structurally below slower horizons.
// • REG BODY is therefore a full-stack measurement, not simply the distance between two averages.
//
// 2) ATR14 NORMALIZATION
// • The signed REG BODY spread is divided by ATR14.
// • This converts the raw price-distance measurement into volatility-relative units so the engine can
//   behave more consistently across symbols, prices, and timeframes.
//
// 3) SOFT PEAK-PERSISTENCE ATR-DRAG GUARD
// • A strong, orderly move can appear to weaken simply because ATR expands faster than the ribbon body.
// • The guard watches REG BODY persistence, stack order, and ATR expansion together.
// • When structure remains highly ordered and the ribbon body is still holding/expanding, the guard can
//   temporarily preserve part of the prior normalized strength instead of allowing an ATR spike to collapse it.
// • The effect is capped and decays automatically. It releases when directional side changes, order deteriorates,
//   the ribbon body cools, or the qualifying structural conditions are no longer present.
//
// 4) WIDE SEMANTIC — signed structural-strength scale
// • The guarded ATR-normalized REG BODY is mapped to a bounded -100…+100 scale.
// • The mapping is intentionally non-linear so ordinary trends retain useful separation while increasingly
//   uncommon structural expansion is pushed toward the outer readings.
// • Key absolute-value anchors:
//      0.70 ATR → 34
//      1.25 ATR → 55
//      2.50 ATR → 65
//      4.00 ATR → 75
//      7.00 ATR → 89
//      12.0 ATR → 95
//      20.0 ATR → 100
// • Positive values indicate bullish structural direction; negative values indicate bearish direction.
// • CORE in the table is this final signed Wide Semantic value. It is a structural-strength reading,
//   not a probability, price target, or percentage.
//
// GLOBAL REGIME ENGINE
// • Bull Rise — accepted bullish full-stack structure.
// • Bear Fall — accepted bearish full-stack structure.
// • Bull Resistance — prior bullish lineage remains active while the full bullish stack is disrupted.
// • Bear Support — prior bearish lineage remains active while the full bearish stack is disrupted.
// • Top / Bottom Extreme and Exceptional states identify unusually large same-direction structural expansion.
// • Structural ownership uses fixed Wide Semantic rails:
//      same-side full-stack re-entry = ±34
//      opposite/initial directional transfer = ±55
//      Extreme entry / release = ±89 / ±75
//      Exceptional entry / release = ±95 / ±89
// • Extreme and Exceptional persistence also require the corresponding full stack to remain physically intact.
//
// RIBBON + TRANSITION RENDERING
// • The visible ribbon contains five adjacent bands:
//      5/8 → 8/13 → 13/20 → 20/34 → 34/50.
// • Gradient mode uses opaque background-matched shades so crossover bands can cover one another cleanly
//   without transparent-fill discoloration.
// • Foreground transition ownership propagates contiguously from the fast 5/8 edge.
// • A deeper band cannot visually change direction until every faster pair in front of it has aligned first.
// • Bull Resistance rollover and Bear Support recovery/rollover use the same contiguous pair-by-pair ownership,
//   allowing the ribbon to show transition progression instead of flipping every band at once.
// • Global Regime mode is also available for a flat single-color presentation.
//
// PLOTCANDLES + PRICE FOLLOW
// • Optional PlotCandles use the active Global Regime color with independent body, wick, and border transparency.
// • The hardcoded Bar-to-Bar Follow Line uses native show_last=2, producing one previous-close → current-close
//   segment colored by the active Global Regime.
//
// RIGHT-SIDE OHLC LABELS
// • OHLC5 / 8 / 13 / 20 / 34 / 50 labels inherit the active ribbon presentation at their physical gradient boundaries.
// • Internal labels use interpolated boundary shades so the right-label stack visually continues the ribbon gradient.
// • A label-only brightness lift improves readability without changing the ribbon itself.
// • Each level independently tracks the most recent live price-side ownership:
//      $⤵ on the TOP row = price most recently moved from above to below that OHLC level;
//      $⤴ on the BOTTOM row = price most recently moved from below to above that OHLC level.
// • The arrow persists until the opposite side takes ownership and can flip within the same live bar.
// • OHLC75 / OHLC110 labels use the separate long-structure color owner:
//      75 > 110 = orange; otherwise = gray.
//
// CROSSOVER EVENT LABELS
// • 5 / 8 = fast-edge crossover.
// • 8 / 20 = optional early-intermediate crossover; default HIDE.
// • 13 / 34 = optional middle-structure crossover; default HIDE.
// • 20 / 50 = slower ribbon-structure crossover.
// • 75 / 110 = long structural crossover.
// • Bullish events print below the candle; bearish events print above the candle.
// • Historical event labels retain the Global Regime color that was active on the bar where the crossover formed.
//
// RIBBON ORDER TELEMETRY
// • ORDER % measures how efficiently the six averages form one monotonic directional path:
//      |OHLC5 − OHLC50| ÷ sum of all five adjacent-pair distances × 100.
// • 100% means the stack is perfectly monotonic from fast to slow.
// • Lower readings indicate increasing internal folding / crossover geometry.
// • Bull/Bear x/5 shows how far the current fast-edge ordering has propagated CONTIGUOUSLY through the five pairs.
// • ORDER telemetry describes current geometry only; it does not override Global Regime ownership.
//
// DEVELOPING HTF CORE
// • The table also calculates the same six-RMA CORE engine natively on the automatically selected next higher timeframe.
// • This is a DEVELOPING reading: gaps_off, lookahead_off, no confirmed-bar [1] offset.
// • Because it uses the live higher-timeframe candle, the HTF CORE value can continue changing until that HTF candle closes.
// • The chart-timeframe and HTF readings use the same REG BODY, ATR normalization, guard, and Wide Semantic architecture.
//
// LONG STRUCTURAL PAIR
// • OHLC75 and OHLC110 are separate RMA(OHLC4) structural plots.
// • They do not participate in the 5/8/13/20/34/50 REG BODY, Global Regime, or ribbon transition ownership.
// • Both long plots and both long right labels share one state color:
//      75 > 110 = orange; otherwise = gray.
// • The table shows the active long-pair order and inclusive bars since the most recent 75/110 crossover.
//
// CONTEXT TABLE
// • Row 1:
//      Ticker / chart timeframe
//      → Global Regime + inclusive regime age
//      → Ribbon ORDER % + contiguous Bull/Bear x/5
//      → Chart CORE
//      → Developing Auto-Next-HTF CORE.
// • Row 2:
//      Current 75 / 110 order
//      → inclusive bars since the most recent 75/110 crossover.
// • Both rows include hover tooltips that explain the displayed readings.
//
// PERFORMANCE / IMPLEMENTATION
// • Stateful RMA, ATR, and crossover kernels execute continuously for Pine consistency.
// • Presentation work is gated independently from calculation state.
// • Developing HTF CORE uses one request.security call.
// • Right-label updates and context-table updates are last-bar managed.
// • Historical crossover labels rebuild only within their enabled Last-N windows.
// • Ribbon and follow-line history use native show_last where appropriate.
// • No line-object family is used.
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Script Overview
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Constants
// ==============================================================================================

const string SHOW = "Show"
const string HIDE = "Hide"

const string LABEL_PADDING_GROUPED = "Grouped"
const string LABEL_PADDING_INDIVIDUAL = "Individual"
const string CHANGE_LAYOUT_ROWS = "Different Rows"
const string CHANGE_LAYOUT_INLINE = "Side by Side"

const int OHLC_LEN_1 = 5
const int OHLC_LEN_2 = 8
const int OHLC_LEN_3 = 13
const int OHLC_LEN_4 = 20
const int OHLC_LEN_5 = 34
const int OHLC_LEN_6 = 50
const int OHLC_LONG_FAST_LEN = 75
const int OHLC_LONG_SLOW_LEN = 110
const int OHLC_STACK_COUNT = 6
const int OHLC_BAND_COUNT = 5
const int OHLC_ATR_LEN = 14
const int MAX_CROSS_SCAN_BARS = 500
const int MAX_CROSS_LABEL_OBJECTS = 488

// Structural ownership rails used by the Global Regime engine.
const float OHLC_REENTRY_THRESHOLD = 34.0
const float OHLC_TRANSFER_THRESHOLD = 55.0
const float OHLC_EXTREME_THRESHOLD = 89.0
const float OHLC_EXTREME_RELEASE_THRESHOLD = 75.0
const float OHLC_EXCEPTIONAL_THRESHOLD = 95.0
const float OHLC_EXCEPTIONAL_RELEASE_THRESHOLD = 89.0

// RMA theoretical-lag regression coordinates for 5/8/13/20/34/50.
// Wilder RMA low-frequency lag = N - 1, yielding 4/7/12/19/33/49.
const float OHLC_REG_LAG_MEAN = 20.666666666666668
const float OHLC_REG_LAG_SS = 1497.3333333333333
const float OHLC_REG_LAG_SPAN = 45.0

// Frozen Soft Peak-Persistence ATR-Drag Guard.
const float OHLC_REG_PEAK_DECAY = 0.991
const float OHLC_GUARD_MIN_PK_PCT = 90.0
const float OHLC_GUARD_MIN_ORDER = 90.0
const float OHLC_GUARD_MIN_RAW = 2.50
const float OHLC_GUARD_FLOOR_DECAY = 0.991
const float OHLC_GUARD_MAX_BLEND = 0.85
const float OHLC_GUARD_STRENGTH_DECAY = 0.92
const float OHLC_GUARD_FULL_DRAG_PCT = 20.0

// Canonical production-look five-band transparency ladder.
const int OHLC_BAND_1_TRANSP = 58
const int OHLC_BAND_2_TRANSP = 66
const int OHLC_BAND_3_TRANSP = 74
const int OHLC_BAND_4_TRANSP = 82
const int OHLC_BAND_5_TRANSP = 88

const color INVISIBLE_COLOR = #00000000
const string OHLC_PRICE_CROSS_DOWN_ARROW = "$⤵"
const string OHLC_PRICE_CROSS_UP_ARROW = "$⤴"
const color OHLC_LONG_BULL_LABEL_COLOR = #ff8400
const color OHLC_LONG_BEAR_LABEL_COLOR = color.rgb(135, 135, 135)

// 🔹 Canonical hardcoded price Bar-to-Bar Follow Line
const int OHLC_BAR_TO_BAR_FOLLOW_LAST_N = 2
const int OHLC_BAR_TO_BAR_FOLLOW_WIDTH = 2
const int OHLC_BAR_TO_BAR_FOLLOW_TRANSP = 0

const string G_VIS = "OHLC Ribbon Visuals"
const string G_CANDLES = "OHLC PlotCandles"
const string G_COLORS = "OHLC Ribbon Regime Colors"
const string G_LABELS = "Right-Side OHLC Labels"
const string G_LONG = "Long Structural OHLC"
const string G_TABLE = "OHLC Context Table"
const string G_CROSS = "OHLC Crossover Labels"

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Constants
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Tooltip Strings
// ==============================================================================================

const string TT_RIBBON =
     "Shows the fixed RMA(OHLC4) 5/8/13/20/34/50 structural ribbon.\n\n" +
     "The six-average stack drives the REG BODY, Wide Semantic CORE, Global Regime colors, and contiguous transition renderer described in the Script Overview."

const string TT_RIBBON_COLOR =
     "Controls the OHLC Ribbon presentation.\n\n" +
     "• Gradient — default. Uses the canonical opaque production-look five-band gradient plus contiguous crossover foreground ownership.\n" +
     "• Global Regime — paints all five bands with the exact active regime color."

const string TT_PLOT_CANDLES =
     "Overlays native OHLC price candles colored by the exact resolved OHLC global-regime engine.\n\n" +
     "Body, wick, and border transparency are independent. Set any component to 100 to make only that component fully transparent.\n\n" +
     "This is presentation-only: no additional rolling kernels, requests, lines, labels, or tables are created."

const string TT_RIGHT_LABELS =
     "Master gate for the eight OHLC right-side labels.\n\n" +
     "OHLC5/8/13/20/34/50 inherit the active Ribbon color engine at their physical gradient boundary, including transition ownership. Gradient mode interpolates the two neighboring visible band shades at internal MA boundaries, then applies a label-only Brightness + lift so the text remains readable without changing the ribbon itself. Global Regime mode stays flat. Each label independently latches the last close-vs-level ownership: $⤵ on the top row means price most recently moved below that OHLC level; $⤴ on the bottom row means price most recently moved above it. The $ identifies the cue as price-relative-to-level telemetry, and the arrow persists until the opposite side takes ownership.\n\n" +
     "OHLC75/110 retain their shared long-pair state color: orange while 75 > 110, gray otherwise.\n\n" +
     "Labels are independent from Ribbon visibility. Formatting and label-object updates are last-bar gated."

const string TT_RIGHT_LABEL_PADDING =
     "Controls dynamic right-label spacing.\n\n" +
     "Individual — DEFAULT. Every visible OHLC label owns its own horizontal lane.\n" +
     "Grouped — all visible OHLC labels share one lane.\n\n" +
     "Only visible labels consume Individual spacing. No bar_index offset is used."

const string TT_RIGHT_LABEL_LAYOUT =
     "Controls how dollar and percent distance appear beneath each OHLC tag.\n\n" +
     "Different Rows is the default."

const string TT_LONG_STRUCT =
     "Separate long structural RMA(OHLC4) pair.\n\n" +
     "OHLC75 and OHLC110 are plotted as independent structural lines and do NOT participate in the 5/8/13/20/34/50 regime engine, REG BODY, or ribbon transition ownership.\n\n" +
     "OHLC75 / OHLC110 plots and right labels share ONE resolved long-pair state color: orange while 75 > 110, gray otherwise.\n\n" +
     "The pair has its own 75/110 crossover event family under OHLC Crossover Labels."

const string TT_TABLE =
     "Compact two-row context table for the short ribbon and long structural pair.\n\n" +
     "Row 1 = Ticker / chart TF, OHLC Global Regime + inclusive age, short-ribbon ORDER %, contiguous fast-edge propagation x/5, Chart CORE, and Developing Auto-Next-HTF CORE on the bottom line.\n" +
     "Row 2 = the separate OHLC75/110 long structural pair shown as the actual current order (75 > 110 or 110 > 75) plus inclusive crossover age, using the exact same orange/gray color owner as both long plots and right labels.\n\n" +
     "Developing HTF CORE uses the same six-RMA REG BODY / ATR14 / guard / Wide Semantic architecture calculated natively on the next higher timeframe with lookahead_off. It can continue changing until that HTF candle closes."

const string TT_CROSS =
     "Shows OHLC-stack crossover events using the fixed RMA(OHLC4) series.\n\n" +
     "OHLC 5/8 is the fast-edge pair and the same pair that arms Bull Resistance rollover ownership.\n" +
     "OHLC 8/20 is an optional early-intermediate crossover and defaults HIDE.\n" +
     "OHLC 13/34 is an optional middle-structure crossover and defaults HIDE.\n" +
     "OHLC 20/50 is the slower ribbon-structure crossover.\n" +
     "OHLC 75/110 is the separate long structural crossover.\n\n" +
     "Bullish crossovers are always BELOW the candle. Bearish crossovers are always ABOVE the candle.\n" +
     "Each event label inherits the exact OHLC Global Regime color resolved on the bar where that crossover formed.\n" +
     "The two-row text lists the newly-leading average first."

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Tooltip Strings
